{"id": "EUVD-2026-103517", "enisaUuid": "b940435e-4cf9-3d52-a3e3-e6bf7be33acf", "description": "wvWare wv through 1.2.9 contains a stack-based out-of-bounds read vulnerability in wvGetPAPX_FKP and wvGetCHPX_FKP caused by an unvalidated FKP run count. Attackers can supply a crafted .doc file with a large crun value to read kilobytes past the 512-byte stack buffer, crashing applications like AbiWord.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T12:19:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T16:29:54", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/wv-fkp-crun-stsh-cstd-oob-read", "https://github.com/AbiWord/wv/blob/wv-1-2-9/fkp.c#L122", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/wvware-wv-through-1.2.9-stack-out-of-bounds-read-via-wvgetpapx-fkp-and-wvgetchpx-fkp"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jf7v-2r7w-h9p9", "CVE-2026-112055"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d86fd9eb-39ab-3555-a0d1-e5f4f0b0302f", "product": {"name": "wv", "vendor": {"name": "wvWare"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.2.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4b3142fe-d177-326d-b669-f9e5237641f7", "vendor": {"name": "wvWare"}}], "isExploited": false}